\section{Monte Carlo Phase-Space Clouds}

For $N_{\text{MC}}$ replicates:
\[
\gamma_{XY}^{(n)}
=
\big\{
\pi_{XY}^{(n)}(t) : t \in [t_0, t_f]
\big\},
\quad
n = 1,\dots,N_{\text{MC}}.
\]

We define the phase-space density:
\[
\rho_{XY}(x,y)
=
\frac{1}{N_{\text{MC}}}
\sum_{n=1}^{N_{\text{MC}}}
\int_{t_0}^{t_f}
\delta\big(x - X^{(n)}(t)\big)
\delta\big(y - Y^{(n)}(t)\big)\, dt.
\]

\section{Collapse Threshold Maps}

Define a collapse indicator:
\[
C(t)
=
\mathbb{1}
\big(
H(t) < H_{\text{thr}}
\lor
A(t) < A_{\text{thr}}
\lor
s(t) > s_{\text{thr}}
\big).
\]

We map initial conditions $(P_0, H_0, s_0)$ to collapse probability:
\[
\Pi_{\text{collapse}}(P_0, H_0, s_0)
=
\frac{1}{N_{\text{MC}}}
\sum_{n=1}^{N_{\text{MC}}}
C^{(n)}(t_f).
\]

\section{Summary}

Full system phase-space trajectories reveal the emergent geometry of the
MPS--PCE engine: attractors, collapse manifolds, resilience basins, and
critical thresholds. These projections turn the raw simulation into a
visualizable dynamical landscape that physicists, scientists, and engineers
can interrogate directly.